<p>1883 East Main St (Merchants Hotel in center) Herman Yunck, Henry's younger brother, was born in 1854 in Richmond, MN. He moved to Mandan in 1881 and worked for D.R. Taylor (druggist) and the NP Railway. He was also employed on various riverboats for several years before operating a saloon owned by Henry. Henry died in April 1884. Herman married his brother's widow Philomena in 1886 and continued to operate the hotel with her. Together, they raised a total of six of Philomena's seven children. Herman was a charter member of the Mandan volunteer fire department; running the Hook and Ladder Company. He died on September 23, 1913. Pallbearers at his funeral included early city leaders including D.R. Taylor, Charles Wyman, John Foran, Pat Tobin, H. L. Henke and George Bingenheimer.</p>

